  "worked_solution": "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give $2+(-5)=2-5.$ \n\nThen, we move $5$ spaces to the left of $2$ on a number line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149424/assets/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nWe end up at $-3.$ So, $2+(-5)=-3.$",
